# Process lifecycle

This craft is a **long-lived device daemon**, typically under **systemd** (or
equivalent service manager). It is not a one-shot CLI and not a bootloader /
pre-boot agent.

## Hard rules

1. Separate **construction** (cheap, sync) from **run** (async/event loop) —
   same spirit as python-services DI construct vs `initialize`.
2. Clean shutdown on SIGTERM: flush bounded queues, close IPC, release host
   resources without silent swallow (**`fail-fast.mdc`**).
3. Crash restart policy is ops/unit file — document in consumer deploy docs;
   constitution requires the process be restart-safe (idempotent startup).

